WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.801 --> 00:00:01.868
-Who is better?

00:00:01.868 --> 00:00:03.801
Who is better than Miley Cyrus?

00:00:03.801 --> 00:00:06.634
-You always decide how
the show kind of goes,

00:00:06.634 --> 00:00:09.067
what we're going to do,
and how it's going to flow.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.033
And I don't know if everyone
gets to sit

00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:13.601
and tell you how much
they appreciate you

00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:14.834
and sitting on your couch.

00:00:14.834 --> 00:00:17.534
You are one of my favorite
people to talk to.

00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:18.934
And when I come to New York,

00:00:18.934 --> 00:00:22.000
I look forward to coming
and sitting and talking to you.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.200
You make everyone feel so good,
so comfortable.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.234
The Roots always sound amazing.

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:28.300
This is the most fun show.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you for saying that.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:31.701
-You tell everyone,
"You're the best.

00:00:31.701 --> 00:00:33.033
Miley Cyrus, everybody."

00:00:33.033 --> 00:00:35.067
He's always announcing everyone.

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.534
You are just so fun
to come and see.

00:00:36.534 --> 00:00:37.934
I just feel so happy to be here.

00:00:37.934 --> 00:00:40.400
-I legitimately think
you are the best.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.734
-I think you are.

00:00:41.734 --> 00:00:43.501
-We've had Miley Week here --

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:46.267
-I can't believe
you let me do that.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:49.300
I came out, and I saw
your audience before the show.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.801
And I don't even know --
I don't think I was --

00:00:52.801 --> 00:00:54.601
Why was I here for a whole week?
-I don't know.

00:00:54.601 --> 00:00:56.033
There was no reason.
-I don't even know

00:00:56.033 --> 00:00:57.367
if I had
an album or anything.

00:00:57.367 --> 00:00:58.634
I think I just said, "Jimmy,

00:00:58.634 --> 00:01:00.334
can I be on your show
for a full week?"

00:01:00.334 --> 00:01:02.033
And you said, "Yeah,

00:01:02.033 --> 00:01:04.567
uh, do you want to open
for Hillary Clinton?"

00:01:04.567 --> 00:01:05.567
-Oh, yeah.
-She was here.

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.167
-Hillary was here.
We did sketches.

00:01:07.167 --> 00:01:09.167
-"Boots Are Made for Walking."
We did sketches.

00:01:09.167 --> 00:01:11.434
I got to perform with Sandler.

00:01:11.434 --> 00:01:14.200
It was such a --
I don't know why I was here.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.701
-I have no idea
why you were here.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.234
-I got to play with,
you know, The Roots.

00:01:17.234 --> 00:01:19.400
-But you were very nice.
You were nice to everybody.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.834
And everyone on your team was
nice to everyone on our crew.

00:01:22.834 --> 00:01:24.167
It just gelled.
It was awesome.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:25.801
By the end of the week,
we were all almost in tears

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:27.200
that you were leaving
because we were like,

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:30.434
"She's so fun,"
and we were going to miss you.

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:31.834
As you were leaving,
you were like, "By the way,

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:33.767
I just donated
all this money to your charity."

00:01:33.767 --> 00:01:35.467
And I go, "Thank you
for doing that."

00:01:35.467 --> 00:01:37.434
-Great people that do
great things

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:39.334
are my favorite kind of people.
-But you did it.

00:01:39.334 --> 00:01:41.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
That was the extra move.

00:01:41.467 --> 00:01:42.567
You're like...

00:01:42.567 --> 00:01:44.534
Just sunk a three-pointer
on the way out.

00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:45.901
I loved it.
-I love it.

00:01:45.901 --> 00:01:47.000
-Let's talk about
New Year's Eve.

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.534
-Yeah.
-Okay, this is giant.

00:01:48.534 --> 00:01:49.701
You're back in Miami?

00:01:49.701 --> 00:01:51.734
-Yes, I'm back in Miami.
-Ooh, I love it.

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:53.767
Last year was unbelievable.

00:01:53.767 --> 00:01:55.801
-I refuse to be cold,

00:01:55.801 --> 00:01:59.567
and I've learned my lesson
in this building

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:00.734
that it is always freezing.

00:02:00.734 --> 00:02:03.234
So, I was cold,
so I'm wearing gloves.

00:02:03.234 --> 00:02:05.601
-We like to keep it cold here.
-They are extremely fashionable

00:02:05.601 --> 00:02:06.868
and sickening,

00:02:06.868 --> 00:02:08.868
but they're also
for functionality.

00:02:08.868 --> 00:02:10.701
I am freezing.
-Yeah.

00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:12.000
-So, I -- you know,

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.467
Dolly Parton
is my co-host this year.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:15.767
-Now, come on,
That's -- Dolly.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:17.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:19.067
-Yeah.
I called Dolly,

00:02:19.067 --> 00:02:20.534
and I asked her,
"Would you do New Year's?"

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.868
And she goes, "Miley, I want to,
but I just can't be cold.

00:02:22.868 --> 00:02:24.400
I can't go to New York
for New Year's."

00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:25.667
I said, "It's not in New York.

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:27.234
It's in Miami.
It's going to be warm.

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:28.434
We can wear little clothes."

00:02:28.434 --> 00:02:30.968
And she said, "I'm in."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.968 --> 00:02:32.667
-I mean, come on.
-She is the best.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.801
-Here's you and Dolly.
This is the shot.

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:35.968
-Me and my fairy Godmother.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:37.734
-That's it. That's right.

00:02:37.734 --> 00:02:39.200
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:43.167
She's one of the most charming,
funniest --

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:45.167
She's one of the --
She's a pro.

00:02:45.167 --> 00:02:46.400
-She really is.
-She just knows.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.801
She's like, "Yeah,
what are we going to do?

00:02:47.801 --> 00:02:49.167
Hit that mark and do this."

00:02:49.167 --> 00:02:50.334
And then she'll surprise me
with a joke.

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:51.968
-And talking
about the kindness.

00:02:51.968 --> 00:02:55.801
It is like, unparalleled
how gracious she is

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:57.968
in every single room
that she is in.

00:02:57.968 --> 00:02:59.000
-Yes.
-I remember

00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:01.200
when she was on
"Hannah Montana"

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:02.801
and she played my aunt,

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:05.033
she came in
and brought doughnuts

00:03:05.033 --> 00:03:07.200
and Dolly merch for everyone.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.834
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.801
-Here's you and Dolly
from "Hannah Montana."

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:11.968
-Yep.

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.601
-And she was on our show.

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:15.501 --> 00:03:17.567
I was saying how cool
she was for doing that,

00:03:17.567 --> 00:03:18.901
and she turned it around
and said

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:20.868
how cool you were
to have her on.

00:03:20.868 --> 00:03:22.834
-I know.
She always says that.

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.567
-"Because you introduced me
to a whole new audience."

00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:27.667
-I don't know if Dolly knows
what Dolly is. You know?

00:03:27.667 --> 00:03:29.234
-She's unbelievable.
-She really is.

00:03:29.234 --> 00:03:30.834
-We got to be in
the same movie together.

00:03:30.834 --> 00:03:33.300
-That's right.
And Dolly loves Christmas.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.467
She loves the holidays.

00:03:34.467 --> 00:03:36.133
She's like a little kid
at Christmastime.

00:03:36.133 --> 00:03:37.667
-She's perfect
for the holidays.

00:03:37.667 --> 00:03:39.834
-When I watched
the "Mountain Magic,"

00:03:39.834 --> 00:03:42.200
and she saw snow
for the first time

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.300
in that opening scene,
I started crying.

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:46.267
-She can act.
-It's the most pure reaction.

00:03:46.267 --> 00:03:47.834
She's not acting.

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:50.601
She loves snow.

00:03:50.601 --> 00:03:53.367
-She's so childlike and fun
and a pro,

00:03:53.367 --> 00:03:54.767
and I danced with her.

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:56.834
I had a scene where I got
to dance with Dolly Parton.

00:03:56.834 --> 00:03:59.534
And I'm not kidding, I danced
with her from 10:00 to 3:00 --

00:03:59.534 --> 00:04:00.767
not 9:00 to 5:00.

00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:01.901
-Ohh.
-But 10:00 to 3:00, I was like,

00:04:01.901 --> 00:04:03.267
"Ah, we're so close."
-So close.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:04.934
-I know. We didn't do it.

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:06.300
-You didn't commit to that joke.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.234
-Have you celebrated
the holidays with Dolly before?

00:04:09.234 --> 00:04:11.167
-We haven't really done
Christmas together.

00:04:11.167 --> 00:04:14.634
We always talk around
the holidays, you know?

00:04:14.634 --> 00:04:17.167
I called her the other day
to talk about the show

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:18.300
and what we were going to do.

00:04:18.300 --> 00:04:19.834
And I said,
"What are you doing, Dolly?"

00:04:19.834 --> 00:04:21.000
She said, "Well, I'm sitting
at home,

00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.667
and I'm signing
all my Christmas cards."

00:04:22.667 --> 00:04:24.400
I go, "Okay,
I'm doing it tomorrow."

00:04:24.400 --> 00:04:26.434
And she goes, "Well,
I'm doing it right now."

00:04:26.434 --> 00:04:27.868
She's very competitive.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.534
-She's like, "Yeah,
I'm doing it right now."

00:04:29.534 --> 00:04:33.167
-"I'll do it tomorrow."
"Well, I'm doing it now."

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:34.968
-Can you say what you have
planned, or who's performing?

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:37.133
I know you're going to sing.
-So, Dolly told me

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:38.868
she wanted to do
something different

00:04:38.868 --> 00:04:40.701
that she had never done before.

00:04:40.701 --> 00:04:42.434
And what I think
I love about that

00:04:42.434 --> 00:04:44.901
is a lot of people
feel that way around New Year's.

00:04:44.901 --> 00:04:46.267
That resonates.

00:04:46.267 --> 00:04:48.834
I think everybody knows when
the clock turns midnight,

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:51.200
they think that we're all
going to magically change.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.167
But nothing changes
unless you change,

00:04:53.167 --> 00:04:57.033
unless you are making
those choices to be different.

00:04:57.033 --> 00:04:58.934
And so, Dolly being different,

00:04:58.934 --> 00:05:01.601
I'm convinced it's going to be
the same silhouette we've had

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:02.968
since, you know --

00:05:02.968 --> 00:05:05.300
I don't know how different
it's going to get.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.133
If Dolly shows up an "A" cup,

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.300
which I don't think
is happening...

00:05:09.300 --> 00:05:12.334
and a little brunette haircut --
I don't think it's happening.

00:05:12.334 --> 00:05:16.267
So, I sent her a pair of some
leopard gloves that I had.

00:05:16.267 --> 00:05:17.834
And I said,
"I think we can work off that."

00:05:17.834 --> 00:05:19.968
And she sent me back
some leopard hair.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:22.434
She's always got to one-up.

00:05:22.434 --> 00:05:25.167
-And who is performing?
Can we say?

00:05:25.167 --> 00:05:27.801
-So, right now, Sia is coming.

00:05:27.801 --> 00:05:28.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:28.934 --> 00:05:30.968
She's one of my favorite --
-I love Sia.

00:05:30.968 --> 00:05:32.300
-She's one of my favorite
artists.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:35.601
And I love as many wigs
as we can have as possible.

00:05:35.601 --> 00:05:36.834
So, we have Sia.
-Yeah.

00:05:36.834 --> 00:05:38.667
-We have Latto.

00:05:38.667 --> 00:05:40.434
Rae Sremmurd,
who are friends of mine.

00:05:40.434 --> 00:05:41.434
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:41.434 --> 00:05:42.868
-As we get closer to the show,

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:44.534
I want to start revealing
who else we have.

00:05:44.534 --> 00:05:46.701
But the lineup is very me.

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:50.400
It is curated in a way
that makes no sense,

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.901
but makes total sense.

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:54.467
-I don't know how you pulled it
off, though, when you did it,

00:05:54.467 --> 00:05:55.834
because it was COVID.

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:57.067
It was just getting
out of COVID.

00:05:57.067 --> 00:05:58.434
It was just tricky.

00:05:58.434 --> 00:05:59.701
Everyone was like,
"I don't know

00:05:59.701 --> 00:06:01.033
if you're going to
pull this off."

00:06:01.033 --> 00:06:04.634
-Lorne Michaels makes magic.
-Lorne is great.

00:06:04.634 --> 00:06:07.868
-We get there,
and COVID was happening.

00:06:07.868 --> 00:06:10.200
And we wanted to do the most
responsible thing

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:11.334
that we could do.

00:06:11.334 --> 00:06:13.300
We really -- We had barely
any audience.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:16.067
I just had a couple friends
and my own family members there.

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:18.100
We had kind of thought
of everything,

00:06:18.100 --> 00:06:19.868
except that
the Telemundo Studios

00:06:19.868 --> 00:06:21.400
is right by the airport.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.000
We didn't think about that part.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:24.400
And planes kept going by.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.868
And that was really what was
starting to ruin the show.

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:28.701
And somehow,
Lorne Michaels called

00:06:28.701 --> 00:06:32.701
and got all air traffic
to stop before the air...

00:06:32.701 --> 00:06:34.133
[ Laughter ]
-What?

00:06:34.133 --> 00:06:36.200
-...so no planes could fly
overhead while we did our show.

00:06:36.200 --> 00:06:37.701
-I never heard this story.

00:06:37.701 --> 00:06:39.167
-Everyone now when they realize

00:06:39.167 --> 00:06:40.601
that their holiday plans
were ruined

00:06:40.601 --> 00:06:42.167
because they had
to fly over Miami

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:43.334
and they had major delays

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:44.334
hate me.

00:06:44.334 --> 00:06:45.400
[ Laughter ]

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.067
-You or Lorne.
-It's not me. It's Lorne.

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:48.534
-It's Lorne.
Yeah, it's Lorne.

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:49.634
I'm looking forward to it.

00:06:49.634 --> 00:06:50.968
It's a must watch.

00:06:50.968 --> 00:06:52.667
And I'm so happy
you're doing New Year's again.

00:06:52.667 --> 00:06:53.901
It's going to be fantastic.

00:06:53.901 --> 00:06:55.400
-If you feel like being
in Miami for New Year's,

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.467
you're more than welcome --
you all always are.

00:06:57.467 --> 00:06:58.801
-I can always bring the...

00:06:58.801 --> 00:07:01.400
Roots, ready to get on a bus
and see what we can do?

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.434
-Well, I take this seriously,

00:07:03.434 --> 00:07:05.634
so, you know, we'll talk
about it after the show.

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:07.267
But you're welcome
for any New Years.

00:07:07.267 --> 00:07:08.934
For anything I ever do,
you're always welcome.

00:07:08.934 --> 00:07:10.734
You all are.
I just love it so much.

00:07:10.734 --> 00:07:13.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.901 --> 00:07:16.100
-Miley, I have a big question.
-Oh, what's up?

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:17.501
-I have a big question for you.

00:07:17.501 --> 00:07:19.000
And I don't know if you heard,

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.133
but I'm making
a decision tonight,

00:07:20.133 --> 00:07:21.400
a big change.

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:22.601
Like you said, we're always
looking for change.

00:07:22.601 --> 00:07:24.033
-The theme.
-It's the theme.

00:07:24.033 --> 00:07:25.634
New Year's Eve, we're looking
for something different,

00:07:25.634 --> 00:07:27.868
and the only change happens
unless you do it.

00:07:27.868 --> 00:07:28.901
-Right.

00:07:28.901 --> 00:07:30.534
-But I would like you
to do it for me.

00:07:30.534 --> 00:07:31.834
[ Laughter ]
-Okay.

00:07:31.834 --> 00:07:33.200
-I want to shave --

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:34.934
I want to shave my beard.

00:07:34.934 --> 00:07:36.767
-Oh, you're sure?
You want to shave your beard?

00:07:36.767 --> 00:07:38.033
What do y'all think?

00:07:38.033 --> 00:07:39.968
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:39.968 --> 00:07:41.567
And you want me
to shave your beard?

00:07:41.567 --> 00:07:42.567
-Would you do it?

00:07:42.567 --> 00:07:43.934
-Absolutely.
-You will do it?

00:07:43.934 --> 00:07:45.000
-Anything you need from me.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.334
-Let's do this.

00:07:47.334 --> 00:07:48.367
-All right.

00:07:48.367 --> 00:07:50.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:54.300
♪♪

00:07:54.300 --> 00:07:58.467
-Miley Cyrus is shaving my beard
when we come back, everybody.

00:07:58.467 --> 00:07:59.300
Come on back.

